---
layout: layouts/base.njk
---
{#
  LOOM landing page.

  Authored as a design and exported as static HTML; this layout is that
  export carried across into the site's build, the same way the Listen2
  page is a bespoke layout under _includes/layouts/. The page's content
  file is src/apps/loom.md, which sets the /loom/ permalink.

  Since the export, the copy has been rewritten by hand and a demo video
  embedded under the hero. These four things changed on the way in:
    1. assets/*.png            -> /assets/loom/*.png
    2. the content container   -> <main id="main-content">, so base.njk's
                                  skip-link has a target
    3. the Google Fonts <link> -> @font-face on self-hosted woff2 below
    4. the four href="#" links -> inert, visibly not-yet-live controls.
                                  Grep LOOM-LINK-PENDING.

  If the design changes, re-export and regenerate rather than editing
  this file by hand — otherwise the two versions drift.
#}
<style>
  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------
     LOOM landing page — self-hosted webfonts.

     The design was authored against fonts.googleapis.com. The site self-
     hosts its webfonts instead (see the Space Grotesk face in
     src/css/main.css), so these are the same two families served from
     /assets/fonts/. Both are variable fonts: one file covers the whole
     weight range the design uses (Archivo 400-700, JetBrains Mono
     400-700). Licences sit beside them as *-OFL.txt.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
  {% include "components/loom-fonts.njk" %}

  /* The design's own base rules, carried across from the export verbatim.
     They come after /css/main.css in the cascade, so they win where the
     site's Tailwind base layer would otherwise reach this page. */
  html, body { margin: 0; padding: 0; background: #0B0C0E; }
  body { font-family: Archivo, "Helvetica Neue", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; }
  a { color: #4CC9F0; text-decoration: none; }
  a:hover { color: #8AD9F5; text-decoration: underline; }
  *:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #7FDBFF; outline-offset: 2px; }
  img { max-width: 100%; }

  /* The site footer (components/footer.njk) lands on this page's dark
     ground, as it does on the Listen2 page. */
  body > footer { color: #6B7078; }

  /* Phone widths. The design was laid out for a desktop window: its nav row
     needs about 470px, and its 32px gutters leave too little room for the
     content. Below 600px the section links give way to GET LOOM alone and the
     gutters narrow. The grids handle themselves: each minmax() floor is
     min(<floor>, 100%), so a column never asks for more than the page has. */
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .loom-nav-link { display: none; }
    .loom-gutter { padding-left: 16px !important; padding-right: 16px !important; }
  }
</style>

<div style="background:#0B0C0E;color:#E8EAED;font-family:Archivo,sans-serif;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;">

  <div style="position:sticky;top:0;z-index:20;background:rgba(11,12,14,0.92);backdrop-filter:blur(12px);border-bottom:1px solid #23262C;">
    <div class="loom-gutter" style="max-width:1240px;margin:0 auto;padding:14px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;">
      <img src="/assets/loom/loom-icon-64.png" alt="" width="30" height="30" style="width:30px;height:30px;border-radius:7px;display:block;flex:none;">
      <div style="font-size:19px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.02em;flex:none;">LOOM</div>
      <div style="flex:1;min-width:0;"></div>
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:26px;">
        <a href="#instruments" class="loom-nav-link" style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.13em;color:#C7CDD4;">INSTRUMENTS</a>
        <a href="#arrange" class="loom-nav-link" style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.13em;color:#C7CDD4;">ARRANGE</a>
        <a href="#mixer" class="loom-nav-link" style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.13em;color:#C7CDD4;">MIXER</a>
        <a href="#record" class="loom-nav-link" style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.13em;color:#C7CDD4;">RECORD</a>
        <a href="/loom/manual/" class="loom-nav-link" style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.13em;color:#C7CDD4;">MANUAL</a>
        <a href="#get" style="padding:9px 20px;border-radius:6px;background:#4CC9F0;color:#08090B;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;">GET LOOM</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <main id="main-content" class="loom-gutter" style="max-width:1240px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 32px;">

    <div style="padding:104px 0 0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:34px;">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;">
        <div style="width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:2px;background:#35D07F;flex:none;"></div>
        <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:0.2em;color:#8A9099;">LIVE LOOPER FOR MACOS</div>
      </div>
      <h1 style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(46px,6.4vw,88px);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.035em;line-height:0.98;max-width:15ch;text-wrap:balance;">A loop station that plays itself.</h1>
      <p style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(18px,2vw,23px);line-height:1.5;color:#C7CDD4;max-width:60ch;text-wrap:pretty;">Record and overdub on five audio tracks like you would on a hardware looper, and loop a synth, drums and a sampler on four more. Then draw the same moves on a timeline, and the song presses its own buttons while you play. It’s one engine underneath, so everything you learn looping live works the same way in the arrangement.</p>
      <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:14px;">
        <!-- ⛔ LINKED STRAIGHT OUT TO GITHUB RELEASES, AND DELIBERATELY NOT THROUGH A REDIRECT
     ON THIS DOMAIN. GitHub Pages is static, so a /loom/download hop could only be a meta-refresh
     page — strictly worse than an anchor, for no gain: unlike /loom/buy, this URL is not compiled
     into any shipped binary, so there is nothing to protect from becoming unchangeable. The
     `latest/download/LOOM.dmg` form resolves to the newest release forever, which is why
     publishing a version needs no edit here. -->
        <a href="{{ releases.latestDmgUrl }}" style="padding:15px 28px;border-radius:8px;background:#35D07F;color:#08090B;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.09em;">DOWNLOAD FOR MACOS</a>
        <!-- ⛔ /loom/buy AND NOT THE POLAR URL. That path is `loom::licence::kPurchaseUrl`,
     compiled into every shipped binary and unchangeable for a copy already sold, so it is the
     one place in the world that names the merchant. Pointing this button at Polar directly
     would leave that redirect exercised only by the in-app button — a path nobody tests until
     it is broken. See src/loom-buy.njk. -->
        <a href="/loom/buy" style="padding:15px 28px;border-radius:8px;background:#171A1F;border:1px solid #2C3038;color:#E8EAED;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.09em;">BUY A LICENCE</a>
        <!-- ⭐ THE VERSION IS ALWAYS LABELLED "LATEST" AND IS NEVER A CHOICE HERE. Both download
             buttons resolve to releases/latest/download, so what this line names is exactly what
             the button gives you — it comes from the same `releases` data, read from the GitHub
             Releases API at build time, so the page cannot advertise a version it does not ship.
             Older builds exist and have permanent addresses, but they live on /loom/version where
             somebody has gone looking for them. Nobody should have to decide which LOOM to
             download on the page whose job is to give them LOOM. -->
        <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;">Latest ({{ releases.latest.version }}) · {{ releases.latest.dmgSize }} · 14-day free trial<br>{% include "components/loom-price.njk" %}<br>Apple Silicon · macOS 13.3+ · <a href="/loom/version">all versions</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- DEMO VIDEO, AS A CLICK-TO-LOAD POSTER. The page used to embed the player directly, which
         fetched about a megabyte of YouTube's JavaScript on every visit, before anybody chose to
         watch, and was the heaviest thing on the page. Now the page draws a self-hosted poster
         (assets/loom/demo-poster.jpg, YouTube's own thumbnail saved once) and swaps in the
         youtube-nocookie.com player, which sets no cookies until play, only when it is pressed.
         Without JavaScript the poster is a link to the video on YouTube. The VideoObject in the
         structured data below names the same video; change both together. -->
    <div style="padding:64px 0 0;">
      <div id="loom-demo" style="position:relative;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;background:#101216;box-shadow:0 40px 120px rgba(0,0,0,0.7);aspect-ratio:16/9;">
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sngb7h791C4" id="loom-demo-play" aria-label="Play the LOOM demo video" style="position:absolute;inset:0;display:block;">
          {% shot "/assets/loom/demo-poster.jpg", "", "(min-width: 1304px) 1240px, calc(100vw - 32px)", true %}
          <span aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute;left:50%;top:50%;width:84px;height:84px;margin:-42px 0 0 -42px;border-radius:50%;background:rgba(11,12,14,0.78);border:1px solid rgba(232,234,237,0.35);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;"><span style="display:block;width:0;height:0;border-style:solid;border-width:15px 0 15px 25px;border-color:transparent transparent transparent #E8EAED;margin-left:6px;"></span></span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <script>
        (function () {
          var link = document.getElementById('loom-demo-play');
          link.addEventListener('click', function (event) {
            event.preventDefault();
            var frame = document.createElement('iframe');
            frame.src = 'https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/sngb7h791C4?rel=0&autoplay=1';
            frame.title = 'LOOM demo video';
            frame.allow = 'accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share';
            frame.referrerPolicy = 'strict-origin-when-cross-origin';
            frame.allowFullscreen = true;
            frame.style.cssText = 'position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;border:0;display:block;';
            link.replaceWith(frame);
            frame.focus();
          });
        })();
      </script>
      <div style="padding:14px 2px 0;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:0.1em;color:#8A9099;">WATCH THE DEMO</div>
    </div>

    <!-- FULL OVERVIEW VIDEO, the same click-to-load poster as the demo above, below it: the demo
         is two minutes and the overview is thirty, and a visitor who has never heard of LOOM is
         likelier to press play on the short one. The poster is the video's own thumbnail
         (assets/loom/overview-poster.jpg). Its VideoObject sits beside the demo's in the
         structured data below; change both together. -->
    <div style="padding:40px 0 0;">
      <div id="loom-overview" style="position:relative;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;background:#101216;box-shadow:0 40px 120px rgba(0,0,0,0.7);aspect-ratio:16/9;">
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=se70SNu-5nA" id="loom-overview-play" aria-label="Play the LOOM full overview video" style="position:absolute;inset:0;display:block;">
          {% shot "/assets/loom/overview-poster.jpg", "", "(min-width: 1304px) 1240px, calc(100vw - 32px)" %}
          <span aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute;left:50%;top:50%;width:84px;height:84px;margin:-42px 0 0 -42px;border-radius:50%;background:rgba(11,12,14,0.78);border:1px solid rgba(232,234,237,0.35);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;"><span style="display:block;width:0;height:0;border-style:solid;border-width:15px 0 15px 25px;border-color:transparent transparent transparent #E8EAED;margin-left:6px;"></span></span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <script>
        (function () {
          var link = document.getElementById('loom-overview-play');
          link.addEventListener('click', function (event) {
            event.preventDefault();
            var frame = document.createElement('iframe');
            frame.src = 'https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/se70SNu-5nA?rel=0&autoplay=1';
            frame.title = 'LOOM full overview video';
            frame.allow = 'accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share';
            frame.referrerPolicy = 'strict-origin-when-cross-origin';
            frame.allowFullscreen = true;
            frame.style.cssText = 'position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;border:0;display:block;';
            link.replaceWith(frame);
            frame.focus();
          });
        })();
      </script>
      <div style="padding:14px 2px 0;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:0.1em;color:#8A9099;">WATCH THE FULL OVERVIEW · 31 MIN</div>
    </div>

    <div style="padding:64px 0 0;">
      <div style="border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;background:#101216;box-shadow:0 40px 120px rgba(0,0,0,0.7);">
        <!-- SCREENSHOTS: captured 2026-09-19, off ~/Desktop/loom-screenshots-2026-09-19.
             The four originals keep their shot-*.png names rather than the capture names,
             because loom.md's `ogImage` points at shot-looper.png and social platforms cache
             an og:image by URL — a rename would orphan every card already scraped. The
             mapping, for the next refresh:
               shot-looper.png       <- loop-view.png
               shot-arrange.png      <- arrange-view-automation.png
               shot-eq.png           <- mixer-eq-effect.png
               shot-delay.png        <- mixer-delay-effect-sync-options.png
               shot-amp.png          <- mixer-amp-effect.png        (new this refresh)
               shot-racks.png        <- effect-rack-presets.png     (new this refresh)
               shot-record-setup.png <- record-setup.png            (new this refresh)
               shot-chorus.png       <- mixer-chorus-effect.png     (copied in, not placed)
               shot-presets.png      <- effect-presets.png          (copied in, not placed)
             The 1.2 refresh, off ~/Desktop/loom-screenshots-instruments-1.2:
               shot-looper.png        <- looper.png                 (replaced: ROWS layout)
               shot-record-setup.png  <- loom-recording-setup-green.png (replaced: instrument rows)
               shot-looper-banks.png  <- looper-view-banks.png      (new; macOS menu and title bar cropped off)
               shot-synth.png         <- synth.png                  (new)
               shot-drums.png         <- drum-instrument-midi-connected.png (new)
               shot-sampler.png       <- sampler-slicer.png         (new)
             The 1.3 refresh, off ~/Desktop/loom-v1.3-screenshots:
               shot-synth.png         <- synth-retake-poly-arp.png  (replaced: ARP NOTES and STRUM)
               shot-tuner.png         <- strobe-tune.png            (new)
               shot-tuner-needle.png  <- needle-tune-2.png          (new)
               shot-tuner-strings.png <- poly-tune.png              (new)
             ⚠️ EVERY ALT HERE MAKES A COUNTABLE CLAIM — "six bands", "thirteen divisions",
             "ten files" — so each was read off the new image before this commit rather than
             carried across. An alt that describes the previous build is worse than a stale
             screenshot: the screenshot is merely old, the alt is untrue, and the only reader
             who gets the untrue one is the reader who cannot see the image. -->
        {% shot "/assets/loom/shot-looper.png", "LOOM’s looper in two rows: five audio tracks above, their rings showing PLAY, DUB, REC, STOPPED and EMPTY, and four instrument tracks below, all playing. A MIDI IN card lists the connected controllers, and the side panel is open on instrument track 4, a sampler" %}
      </div>
      <div style="padding:14px 2px 0;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:0.1em;color:#8A9099;">LOOPER · FIVE AUDIO TRACKS AND FOUR INSTRUMENT TRACKS · EACH RING SHOWS WHAT YOUR NEXT PRESS WILL DO</div>
    </div>

    <div style="padding:112px 0 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(260px,100%),1fr));gap:16px;">
      
        <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:26px 24px 28px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;">
          <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#FF4438;">ONE PRESS</div>
          <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:17px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;line-height:1.25;">No arming</h3>
          <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">The centre of each ring shows what your next press will do. You don’t arm a track first, and there’s no separate play button to find.</div>
        </div>
      
        <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:26px 24px 28px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;">
          <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#FFB020;">THE GRID FOLLOWS YOU</div>
          <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:17px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;line-height:1.25;">Your first loop sets the tempo</h3>
          <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Record a free-length loop with quantize off and LOOM works out the tempo from what you played. The transport keeps rolling, and you don’t press anything extra.</div>
        </div>
      
        <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:26px 24px 28px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;">
          <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#35D07F;">EVERY STATE</div>
          <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:17px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;line-height:1.25;">Readable without colour</h3>
          <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Each ring state has its own arc pattern as well as its own colour. A wedge marks a command that’s queued and waiting to happen.</div>
        </div>
      
        <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:26px 24px 28px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;">
          <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#4CC9F0;">SAMPLE-ACCURATE</div>
          <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:17px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;line-height:1.25;">Same engine both ways</h3>
          <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">The loop station and the arrangement drive the same engine. A region on the timeline does exactly what your hands would have done.</div>
        </div>
      
    </div>

    <div style="padding:128px 0 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(320px,100%),1fr));gap:56px;align-items:start;">
      <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:20px;">
        <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.2em;color:#8A9099;">WHY LOOM</div>
        <h2 style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(30px,3.4vw,42px);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.025em;line-height:1.08;text-wrap:balance;">The last app that did this isn’t around anymore.</h2>
      </div>
      <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:18px;">
        <p style="margin:0;font-size:17.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#C7CDD4;text-wrap:pretty;">There used to be a live-looping-first application where an arrangement could play a looper for you. But it was discontinued years ago. Everything else makes you pick the immediacy of a loop pedal, the structure of a timeline, or trying to force a DAW to behave like a looper.</p>
        <p style="margin:0;font-size:17.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">LOOM gives you both and keeps the hardware-looper experience a first-class citizen. Press a ring button and it records. Draw the same command on a lane and it fires exactly where you drew it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id="instruments" style="scroll-margin-top:88px;padding:128px 0 0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:32px;">
      <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:18px;max-width:74ch;">
        <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.2em;color:#E04AC1;">INSTRUMENTS</div>
        <h2 style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(32px,3.8vw,50px);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.03em;line-height:1.05;text-wrap:balance;">Loop a synth, drums and a sampler via MIDI</h2>
        <p style="margin:0;font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#C7CDD4;text-wrap:pretty;">Four instrument tracks sit beside the five audio tracks. Each one plays LOOM’s own synth, drum machine or sampler from a MIDI keyboard or pad controller, with the same ring, STOP, UNDO and CLEAR as an audio track.</p>
        <p style="margin:0;font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#C7CDD4;text-wrap:pretty;">LOOM loops the notes, not the sound. Change the preset, the kit or any setting while the loop plays, and the loop plays on with the new sound. You never have to play the part again to hear it on a different instrument.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div style="border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;background:#101216;box-shadow:0 40px 120px rgba(0,0,0,0.7);">
          {% shot "/assets/loom/shot-synth.png", "The synth editor docked under a row of all nine track rings, with every section on one page: two oscillators, the filter and its envelope, the amp envelope, two LFOs, VOICE in POLY with UNISON at 2, DETUNE and SPREAD, and the arpeggiator with its grid of rates, NOTES at 2 and STRUM at 46%" %}
        </div>
        <div style="padding:14px 2px 0;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:0.1em;color:#8A9099;">SYNTH · EVERY CONTROL ON ONE PAGE AT FULL SCREEN</div>
      </div>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(320px,100%),1fr));gap:24px;">
        <div>
          <div style="border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;background:#101216;">
            {% shot "/assets/loom/shot-drums.png", "The drum editor with the Trap n Clap kit and the Trap n Crash pattern loaded: a grid of kick, snare, hats, tom and clap, with the playing step lit and hits played between steps drawn where they sound. Below it are the kick’s first layer with a sine source, its envelope, the tube waveguide, and the kit and step controls with BARS set to 4", "(min-width: 1304px) 610px, (min-width: 700px) calc(50vw - 44px), calc(100vw - 32px)" %}
          </div>
          <div style="padding:14px 2px 0;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:0.1em;color:#8A9099;">DRUM MACHINE · THE GRID IS THE LOOP ITSELF</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div style="border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;background:#101216;">
            {% shot "/assets/loom/shot-sampler.png", "The sampler in SLICE mode with one of LOOM’s own recorded takes cut into twelve slices, each slice coloured on the waveform and mapped to its own key from C3 to B3", "(min-width: 1304px) 610px, (min-width: 700px) calc(50vw - 44px), calc(100vw - 32px)" %}
          </div>
          <div style="padding:14px 2px 0;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:0.1em;color:#8A9099;">SAMPLER · SLICE A TAKE AND PLAY IT FROM THE KEYS</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(300px,100%),1fr));gap:16px;padding-top:8px;">

          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#E04AC1;">SYNTH</div>
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">Two oscillators, a filter and an arpeggiator</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Two oscillators with a sub and noise, a filter with four types and its own envelope, two LFOs, glide, unison of up to four voices with detune and stereo spread, and an arpeggiator that steps on the song’s grid. Each step can play one held note, several, or the whole chord, and STRUM spreads them out like a strummed guitar. In full screen every control and a picture of each oscillator, envelope and LFO fit in one view.</div>
          </div>

          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#FFB020;">DRUM MACHINE</div>
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">The grid is the loop itself</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Hits you play on pads show up in the step grid, and steps you click play in the loop, even while it plays. Each step has its own velocity, accent and ratchet. Set the loop to 1, 2, 4 or 8 bars, and a longer loop starts as a copy of the first. Each drum layers two sounds, from a sine or saw to filtered noise, and can ring through a tube or string resonator.</div>
          </div>

          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#35D07F;">SAMPLER</div>
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">Chop a sample and play it from the keys</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Load a WAV or AIFF and play it across the keys, or switch to SLICE and LOOM cuts it at its transients, one slice per key. Click a slice to hear it, and chop again right where you heard it. MONO makes each slice cut off the last, which is what you want for vocal chops.</div>
          </div>

          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#4CC9F0;">RECORD QUANTIZE</div>
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">Quantize you can take back</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">LOOM keeps each take exactly as you played it and quantizes from that while the loop plays. Tighten a loose take after you record it, or set STRENGTH to OFF to hear it the way you played it.</div>
          </div>

          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#FF4438;">PASS BY PASS</div>
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">Undo every overdub, one at a time</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Each overdub on an instrument track is its own pass. UNDO takes them off one at a time, back to the first take, and REDO puts them back.</div>
          </div>

          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#A78BFA;">MIDI INPUTS</div>
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">Pads on one channel, keys on another</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Each instrument track picks its own device and channel, so pads on channel 10 can play the drums while the keys play the synth. An audio track can also record an instrument, which turns a MIDI loop into audio.</div>
          </div>

      </div>
      <p style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;max-width:74ch;text-wrap:pretty;">LOOM’s instruments are its own: 3rd party plug-ins are not supported for stability. There is not currently a piano roll, no MIDI file import or export and no MIDI output.</p>
      <div style="padding-top:16px;">
        <div style="border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;background:#101216;box-shadow:0 40px 120px rgba(0,0,0,0.7);">
          {% shot "/assets/loom/shot-looper-banks.png", "The looper in BANKS layout: the five audio tracks at full size, their rings showing PLAY, DUB, REC, STOPPED and EMPTY, with AUDIO and INST tabs above them that switch to the four instrument tracks" %}
        </div>
        <div style="padding:14px 2px 0;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:0.1em;color:#8A9099;">LOOPER · BANKS LAYOUT · AUDIO OR INSTRUMENT TRACKS AT FULL SIZE</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id="arrange" style="scroll-margin-top:88px;padding:128px 0 0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:32px;">
      <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:18px;max-width:74ch;">
        <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.2em;color:#4CC9F0;">ARRANGE</div>
        <h2 style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(32px,3.8vw,50px);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.03em;line-height:1.05;text-wrap:balance;">Draw the performance. Play over it.</h2>
        <p style="margin:0;font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#C7CDD4;text-wrap:pretty;">Each track has a lane, instrument tracks included, and you draw regions on it with three verbs: <span style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:16px;color:#FF4438;">REC</span>, <span style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:16px;color:#FFB020;">DUB</span> and <span style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:16px;color:#35D07F;">PLAY</span>. Empty space means the track is stopped. This is the part a hardware looper can’t do without MIDI control from an external sequencer.</p>
        <p style="margin:0;font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#C7CDD4;text-wrap:pretty;">Below the regions, automation lanes work the mixer and the instruments while the song plays: faders, pans, mutes, effect parameters and any instrument control. One node can load a whole saved rack into an FX chain, or a synth preset, drum kit or pattern onto an instrument track, and the lane shows its name, so you can read the song as a row of named sections.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;background:#101216;box-shadow:0 40px 120px rgba(0,0,0,0.7);">
        {% shot "/assets/loom/shot-arrange.png", "LOOM’s arrange view: thirteen regions across five track lanes, with automation lanes below for two FX 2 send levels, a main level, a pan, and two rack lanes with sections named Nasty Acoust G2B, Chorus Delay AC and Clean ACG" %}
      </div>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(240px,100%),1fr));gap:28px;padding-top:8px;">
        
          <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;border-top:1px solid #23262C;padding-top:16px;">
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Start from the top or from anywhere</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Play the arrangement from bar 1 or from wherever the playhead is. Jump to a measure during the performance, synced to the beat.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;border-top:1px solid #23262C;padding-top:16px;">
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Mouse or keyboard</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Drag a region to move it, drag an edge to trim it, and drag past the edge of the window to scroll. The arrangement has its own undo on ⌘Z, and one drag is one undo step, even if it pushed three other regions out of the way.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;border-top:1px solid #23262C;padding-top:16px;">
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Zoom and scroll</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Zoom in or out on the arrangement, fit the song to the window, and choose whether the view follows the playhead.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;border-top:1px solid #A78BFA;padding-top:16px;">
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Automate the mixer too</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Any strip’s level on each of its four fader destinations, its pan and mute, each effect slot’s bypass, the effect’s controls, and every control on an instrument. An INPUT lane changes which controller an instrument track listens to, at the bar you choose.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;border-top:1px solid #A78BFA;padding-top:16px;">
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;">A node can load a whole rack</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Drop a saved preset into one slot, or a saved rack across a whole chain, at whatever bar or beat you place it. The lane shows the name of what’s loaded until the next change.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;border-top:1px solid #A78BFA;padding-top:16px;">
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Old songs stay the way you left them</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">A node keeps its own copy of the settings. Edit or delete that preset later and every song that used it still sounds the same.</div>
          </div>
        
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="padding:120px 0 0;">
      <div style="border:1px solid #3A2320;border-radius:14px;background:linear-gradient(180deg,#15100F,#0F1114);padding:clamp(32px,4vw,56px);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:22px;">
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;">
          <div style="width:3px;height:19px;background:#FF4438;flex:none;border-radius:1px;"></div>
          <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.2em;color:#FF6A5E;">ALL OR NOTHING</div>
        </div>
        <h2 style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(28px,3.4vw,44px);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.03em;line-height:1.06;max-width:24ch;text-wrap:balance;">If something’s wrong, you’ll know before you start.</h2>
        <p style="margin:0;font-size:18px;line-height:1.6;color:#C7CDD4;max-width:66ch;text-wrap:pretty;">If any region in the arrangement can’t play correctly, nothing starts. The notice row lists each problem on its own line, in plain English, starting with what to fix. And the log shows you every notice message in the session.</p>
        <p style="margin:0;font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;max-width:66ch;text-wrap:pretty;">Better to find out up front than halfway through the song.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id="mixer" style="scroll-margin-top:88px;padding:128px 0 0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:32px;">
      <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:18px;max-width:74ch;">
        <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.2em;color:#A78BFA;">MIXER &amp; EFFECTS</div>
        <h2 style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(32px,3.8vw,50px);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.03em;line-height:1.05;text-wrap:balance;">A full mixer behind the loops.</h2>
        <p style="margin:0;font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#C7CDD4;text-wrap:pretty;">One switch flips between the banks: loop tracks, instruments, inputs, master and buses. Every strip has eight insert slots, instruments included, every chain runs in stereo, and the mixer state and FX chains save with the song.</p>
        <p style="margin:0;font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#C7CDD4;text-wrap:pretty;">For effects you get a parametric EQ, compressor, delay, reverb, noise gate, chorus, octave, transparent overdrive, cab, guitar amp, harmony, gain and a tuner. Save a single effect as a preset or a whole chain as a rack, and the arrangement can load either one while you play.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;background:#101216;box-shadow:0 40px 120px rgba(0,0,0,0.7);">
        {% shot "/assets/loom/shot-eq.png", "LOOM’s mixer with the effect drawer open on a parametric EQ: the response curve over a live spectrum, six bands from a high pass to a low pass, a cut at 300 Hz and a lift above 3 kHz, in a chain loaded from the Vocal Air rack" %}
      </div>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(300px,100%),1fr));gap:24px;">
        <div style="border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;background:#101216;">
          {% shot "/assets/loom/shot-delay.png", "The effect drawer open on a delay, third in a chain after a parametric EQ and a compressor, with thirteen beat divisions from 1⁄1 down to 1⁄16T and 1⁄8 selected", "(min-width: 1304px) 610px, (min-width: 700px) calc(50vw - 44px), calc(100vw - 32px)" %}
        </div>
        <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:20px;justify-content:center;">
          
            <div style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-start;">
              <div style="width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:2px;background:#A78BFA;flex:none;margin-top:8px;"></div>
              <div style="flex:1;min-width:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px;">
                <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;">See what your effects are doing</h3>
                <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">The EQ draws its six-band response curve over a live spectrum, and the compressor shows its transfer curve next to a gain-reduction meter.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          
            <div style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-start;">
              <div style="width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:2px;background:#4CC9F0;flex:none;margin-top:8px;"></div>
              <div style="flex:1;min-width:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px;">
                <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;">One row of faders, four destinations</h3>
                <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">MAIN, CUE, FX 1 and FX 2. Pick one and every fader in view controls it, so you’re never hunting for a send knob on each strip.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          
            <div style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-start;">
              <div style="width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:2px;background:#35D07F;flex:none;margin-top:8px;"></div>
              <div style="flex:1;min-width:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px;">
                <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;">A headphone mix and two effects buses</h3>
                <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">CUE is taken before the fader, so you can have more vocals or guitar in your ears while the audience gets the right balance from the main mix. The master and the cue each go out their own pair of outputs, whichever you choose.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          
            <div style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-start;">
              <div style="width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:2px;background:#FFB020;flex:none;margin-top:8px;"></div>
              <div style="flex:1;min-width:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px;">
                <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Type exact values</h3>
                <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">You can type a value into any parameter as well as drag it. Type something out of range and LOOM lets you know.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          
            <div style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-start;">
              <div style="width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:2px;background:#E04AC1;flex:none;margin-top:8px;"></div>
              <div style="flex:1;min-width:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px;">
                <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Tempo-synced delay</h3>
                <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Switch the delay from FREE to SYNC, pick a division, and it follows the song’s tempo. You know you’re gonna reach for the dotted eighth note option. There’s a PING PONG mode too. The delay and the reverb both have MOD, for a little dimension in the repeats and the tail.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          
            <div style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-start;">
              <div style="width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:2px;background:#A78BFA;flex:none;margin-top:8px;"></div>
              <div style="flex:1;min-width:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px;">
                <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Harmonies in the key of the song</h3>
                <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Set the key and scale, and the harmony adds one or two voices to what you sing or play, a third, a fifth or an octave away. The intervals follow the scale the way a backing singer’s would, and your own voice comes through on time. For a song that changes key, automate KEY in the arrange view.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px;max-width:74ch;padding-top:40px;">
        <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(24px,2.6vw,32px);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.02em;line-height:1.15;">A tuner in the chain</h3>
        <p style="margin:0;font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#C7CDD4;text-wrap:pretty;">Put the tuner on your input and tune between songs without leaving LOOM. Play one note and read it on a strobe or a needle, or strum all your open strings and see each one at once. It knows standard, drop D, DADGAD, open G, open D, 7-string, 4- and 5-string bass, ukulele and banjo, and turning on MUTE keeps the audience from hearing you tune. With a typical audio interface it reads to about a tenth of a cent.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(300px,100%),1fr));gap:24px;">
        <div style="border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;background:#101216;">
          {% shot "/assets/loom/shot-tuner.png", "The tuner’s strobe reading an A2 one cent sharp, with the Silent Strobe factory preset loaded, MUTE on, STRINGS on AUTO, and a choice of tunings: STANDARD, DROP D, DADGAD, OPEN G, OPEN D, 7-STRING, BASS 4, BASS 5, UKULELE and BANJO", "(min-width: 1304px) 400px, (min-width: 1000px) calc(33vw - 32px), (min-width: 700px) calc(50vw - 44px), calc(100vw - 32px)" %}
        </div>
        <div style="border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;background:#101216;">
          {% shot "/assets/loom/shot-tuner-needle.png", "The tuner’s needle centred on a D3 at 0.4 cents flat, with the note name, the offset and the needle drawn in green", "(min-width: 1304px) 400px, (min-width: 1000px) calc(33vw - 32px), (min-width: 700px) calc(50vw - 44px), calc(100vw - 32px)" %}
        </div>
        <div style="border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;background:#101216;">
          {% shot "/assets/loom/shot-tuner-strings.png", "The tuner after a strum, with a column for each string of standard tuning: low E 1 cent sharp, A 2, D 1, G with no reading, B 3 and high E 4 cents sharp", "(min-width: 1304px) 400px, (min-width: 1000px) calc(33vw - 32px), (min-width: 700px) calc(50vw - 44px), calc(100vw - 32px)" %}
        </div>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:14px 2px 0;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:0.1em;color:#8A9099;">TUNER · STROBE OR NEEDLE FOR ONE NOTE, EVERY STRING WHEN YOU STRUM</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="padding:128px 0 0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:32px;">
      <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:18px;max-width:74ch;">
        <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.2em;color:#A78BFA;">PRESETS &amp; RACKS</div>
        <h2 style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(32px,3.8vw,50px);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.03em;line-height:1.05;text-wrap:balance;">Save a sound. Recall it mid-song.</h2>
        <p style="margin:0;font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#C7CDD4;text-wrap:pretty;">A preset holds one effect’s settings. A rack holds a whole chain: which effect sits in each slot, all their settings, and which slots are bypassed. LOOM comes with a library of both, and the ones you save sit right alongside them. Loading a rack swaps the whole chain at once, and ⌘Z puts it back.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;background:#101216;box-shadow:0 40px 120px rgba(0,0,0,0.7);">
        {% shot "/assets/loom/shot-racks.png", "LOOM’s rack browser over the mixer, listing the factory racks Vocal Air, Guitar Ambient, Drum Glue, Acoustic Stage, G2B, Bass DI, Pad Wash, Octave Lead and Wide Clean, each with chips naming the effects in it, above the user’s own saved racks" %}
      </div>
      <div style="padding:4px 2px 0;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:0.1em;color:#8A9099;">RACK BROWSER · FACTORY AND USER PRESETS · LOADING ONE SWAPS THE WHOLE FX CHAIN</div>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(320px,100%),1fr));gap:24px;padding-top:24px;">
        <div style="border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;background:#101216;">
          {% shot "/assets/loom/shot-amp.png", "The effect drawer open on the guitar amp: CLEAN, CRUNCH and HIGH GAIN models, gain and tight controls, bass, mid, treble and presence, and a closed 4x12 cab, second in a chain after a noise gate", "(min-width: 1304px) 610px, (min-width: 700px) calc(50vw - 44px), calc(100vw - 32px)" %}
        </div>
        <div style="border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;background:#101216;">
          {% shot "/assets/loom/shot-chorus.png", "The effect drawer open on the chorus: rate, depth, sine or triangle shape, one to four voices, and four stereo modes (offset, split, opposed and mono), third in a chain after an amp", "(min-width: 1304px) 610px, (min-width: 700px) calc(50vw - 44px), calc(100vw - 32px)" %}
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(240px,100%),1fr));gap:28px;padding-top:8px;">
        
          <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;border-top:1px solid #23262C;padding-top:16px;">
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Always know what’s loaded</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">The FX drawer header bar reads EDITED when you’ve changed a setting, FACTORY for a preset that ships with LOOM, AUTOMATED when a lane is controlling it, and OVERRIDE when you’ve picked a different one by hand during a performance.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;border-top:1px solid #23262C;padding-top:16px;">
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Each FX chain has its own undo</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">⌘Z undoes changes to the chain you’re working on, separately from the arrangement.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;border-top:1px solid #23262C;padding-top:16px;">
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;">No clicks when you swap</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Change the effect in a slot while audio is running and LOOM fades the old one out and the new one in over 50 ms.</div>
          </div>
        
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id="record" style="scroll-margin-top:88px;padding:128px 0 0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:32px;">
      <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:18px;max-width:74ch;">
        <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.2em;color:#FF4438;">PERFORMANCE RECORDING</div>
        <h2 style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(32px,3.8vw,50px);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.03em;line-height:1.05;text-wrap:balance;">Perform the song. Mix it later.</h2>
        <p style="margin:0;font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#C7CDD4;text-wrap:pretty;">Hit RECORD on the transport and LOOM saves your whole performance as separate WAV files: one per loop track, one per instrument track, one per effects bus, the main mix, and any groups you set up from live inputs or from tracks and buses. Every file starts at the same moment and stays in sync, so you can drop the files into a DAW and it all lines up at zero.</p>
        <p style="margin:0;font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Your takes still save to the song as usual; this is an extra set of files. Play the set once, then balance it against the video later or re-process a guitar that was too loud in the room.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;background:#101216;box-shadow:0 40px 120px rgba(0,0,0,0.7);">
        {% shot "/assets/loom/shot-record-setup.png", "LOOM’s Record setup sheet: three of the five loop tracks and two of the four instrument tracks ticked, each writing its own WAV file, seven files per recording at 2.69 MB/s, and a panel showing 9.7 GB an hour and 2.3 hours of room on the disk" %}
      </div>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(240px,100%),1fr));gap:28px;padding-top:8px;">
        
          <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;border-top:1px solid #23262C;padding-top:16px;">
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;">You choose what goes in which file</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">A group mixes the sources you tick into one stereo file, so you can record your live vocals and instruments to isolated audio files.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;border-top:1px solid #23262C;padding-top:16px;">
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;">See the disk cost up front</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Before you record, LOOM shows the megabytes per second, the number of files, your free space, and how many hours of recording that leaves you.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;border-top:1px solid #23262C;padding-top:16px;">
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Dropouts get logged</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">If the disk can’t keep up, LOOM fills the gap with silence in every file at once so they stay in sync, and writes the time and length to a Markers.txt file you can open in any text editor.</div>
          </div>
        
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="padding:128px 0 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(340px,100%),1fr));gap:48px;align-items:center;">
      <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:20px;">
        <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.2em;color:#35D07F;">FULLY OFFLINE</div>
        <h2 style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(30px,3.6vw,46px);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.03em;line-height:1.05;text-wrap:balance;">The venue’s WiFi isn’t your problem.</h2>
        <p style="margin:0;font-size:17.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#C7CDD4;text-wrap:pretty;">LOOM never connects to the internet, at launch or at any time after. It doesn’t phone home to check your licence, and it doesn’t download anything. There’s no account or activation server. Your licence is checked right on your Mac.</p>
        <p style="margin:0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">The only exceptions are two buttons that open your web browser: one to buy a licence and one to check for the latest version. But these are initiated by you only.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:2px;background:#23262C;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;">
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;padding:22px 20px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:26px;font-weight:700;color:#35D07F;">0</div>
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.13em;line-height:1.5;color:#8A9099;">ACCOUNTS TO MAKE</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;padding:22px 20px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:26px;font-weight:700;color:#35D07F;">0</div>
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.13em;line-height:1.5;color:#8A9099;">ACTIVATION SERVERS</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;padding:22px 20px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:26px;font-weight:700;color:#35D07F;">0</div>
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.13em;line-height:1.5;color:#8A9099;">REQUESTS SENT</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;padding:22px 20px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:26px;font-weight:700;color:#35D07F;">0</div>
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.13em;line-height:1.5;color:#8A9099;">TRACKING</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;padding:22px 20px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:26px;font-weight:700;color:#35D07F;">0</div>
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.13em;line-height:1.5;color:#8A9099;">SEATS TO DEAUTHORISE</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;padding:22px 20px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:26px;font-weight:700;color:#35D07F;">1</div>
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.13em;line-height:1.5;color:#8A9099;">LICENCE FILE</div>
          </div>
        
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="padding:128px 0 0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:40px;">
      <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;max-width:70ch;">
        <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.2em;color:#8A9099;">AND THE REST</div>
        <h2 style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(30px,3.6vw,46px);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.03em;line-height:1.05;text-wrap:balance;">Built for playing live.</h2>
      </div>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(300px,100%),1fr));gap:16px;">
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#FF4438;">LOOPING</div>
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">Every track, quantized in and out</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Start right away or on the next beat, bar or cycle. Stop right away or at the end of the beat, bar or loop. Set it per track or as the song’s default. You can also pre-set a length of up to 32 bars, and the recording closes itself when it gets there.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#FFB020;">LAYERS</div>
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">Overdub or replace, with undo per track</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">SUM keeps every layer. REPLACE records over what’s there as you play. Each track has one level of undo and redo, separate from the arrangement’s.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#35D07F;">MONITORING</div>
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">You hear yourself right away</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Input 1 is live as soon as LOOM opens, and everything else starts muted. You don’t have to arm anything, or even set up a track, first.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#4CC9F0;">INPUTS</div>
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">Panned takes and stereo pairs</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">An input’s pan is recorded into the take, as well as applied to what you hear. Link input 1, 3, 5 or 7 to the next one and the pair becomes a single strip with one effects chain across both channels.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#A78BFA;">YOUR FILES</div>
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">Every audio take is a WAV you can open</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">32-bit float, stereo, at your interface’s sample rate, written the moment the take ends. Songs are folders in ~/Music/LOOM, and performance recordings sit next to them.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#FF4438;">HARDWARE</div>
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">Switch interfaces without restarting</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Your routing carries over when you switch. If a track still has audio on it, LOOM warns you and gives you the option to save first.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#FFB020;">MESSAGES</div>
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">One notice row, with log history</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">It stays the same height whether it’s showing a two-line message or nothing, so the layout never jumps. LOG opens everything LOOM has told you this session, and you can select and copy it.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#35D07F;">ACCESSIBILITY</div>
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">Full keyboard control, with spoken updates</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Every control is labelled and reachable from the keyboard. This is structural to LOOM’s system design and quality checks. New notices and the focused track’s state are announced, and one switch turns that off for a set.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#4CC9F0;">THE MANUAL</div>
            <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">Built into the app</h3>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Press ⌘/ to open it. It’s a PDF on your Mac, not a web page, so it opens even with no WiFi. You can also <a href="/loom/manual/">read it here</a> before you download.</div>
          </div>
        
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="padding:120px 0 0;">
      <div style="border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:14px;background:#0F1114;padding:clamp(30px,3.6vw,48px);display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(300px,100%),1fr));gap:40px;align-items:start;">
        <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;">
          <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.2em;color:#A78BFA;">MIDI</div>
          <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(24px,2.6vw,32px);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.025em;line-height:1.1;">Play it and run it from MIDI.</h3>
          <p style="margin:0;font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Play the synth, drum machine and sampler from any MIDI keyboard or pad controller, and drive every track and the transport from MIDI notes on a channel of their own, 16 by default. Each track, audio or instrument, gets its own octave with the same seven commands in the same order. A MIDI monitor on the bottom bar shows the last message received, in every view, so you can check that LOOM is seeing your controller.</p>
          <p style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">The command map is fixed for now. There’s no MIDI learn and no way to reassign notes yet, but it’s on the roadmap. Commands answer notes only: CC doesn’t control the mixer or effects, and there’s no MIDI clock, MTC or MMC in or out, and no MIDI output. Clear pads are held for a second, so a stray foot can’t wipe a loop. If your controller is set up for LOOM 1.0, switch MIDI MAP to the 1.0 layout.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#23262C;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;">
          
            <div style="background:#121418;padding:12px 16px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;">
              <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:0.06em;color:#C7CDD4;flex:1;min-width:0;">TRACK 1</div>
              <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:#C7CDD4;flex:none;">0 – 6</div>
            </div>
          
            <div style="background:#121418;padding:12px 16px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;">
              <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:0.06em;color:#C7CDD4;flex:1;min-width:0;">TRACK 2</div>
              <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:#C7CDD4;flex:none;">12 – 18</div>
            </div>
          
            <div style="background:#121418;padding:12px 16px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;">
              <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:0.06em;color:#C7CDD4;flex:1;min-width:0;">TRACK 3</div>
              <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:#C7CDD4;flex:none;">24 – 30</div>
            </div>
          
            <div style="background:#121418;padding:12px 16px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;">
              <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:0.06em;color:#C7CDD4;flex:1;min-width:0;">TRACK 4</div>
              <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:#C7CDD4;flex:none;">36 – 42</div>
            </div>
          
            <div style="background:#121418;padding:12px 16px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;">
              <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:0.06em;color:#C7CDD4;flex:1;min-width:0;">TRACK 5</div>
              <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:#C7CDD4;flex:none;">48 – 54</div>
            </div>
          
            <div style="background:#121418;padding:12px 16px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;">
              <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:0.06em;color:#C7CDD4;flex:1;min-width:0;">INST 1</div>
              <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:#E04AC1;flex:none;">72 – 78</div>
            </div>
          
            <div style="background:#121418;padding:12px 16px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;">
              <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:0.06em;color:#C7CDD4;flex:1;min-width:0;">INST 2</div>
              <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:#E04AC1;flex:none;">84 – 90</div>
            </div>
          
            <div style="background:#121418;padding:12px 16px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;">
              <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:0.06em;color:#C7CDD4;flex:1;min-width:0;">INST 3</div>
              <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:#E04AC1;flex:none;">96 – 102</div>
            </div>
          
            <div style="background:#121418;padding:12px 16px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;">
              <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:0.06em;color:#C7CDD4;flex:1;min-width:0;">INST 4</div>
              <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:#E04AC1;flex:none;">108 – 114</div>
            </div>
          
            <div style="background:#121418;padding:12px 16px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;">
              <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:0.06em;color:#C7CDD4;flex:1;min-width:0;">GLOBALS</div>
